{"version":1,"slug":"photosynthesis","topic":"How does photosynthesis work?","level":"beginner","title":"How Photosynthesis Works","summary":"You will understand how plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make their own food and release oxygen.","scopeNote":null,"scenes":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","title":"How does photosynthesis work?","segments":[{"id":"intro-0","narration":"Have you ever wondered how a giant oak tree builds itself out of thin air and sunlight?","sig":"7BSLvys3sPgUjZin0ASXE_XD0UQeQTOr","actions":[{"id":"hero","kind":"icon","cue":"Have you ever","text":"Photosynthesis","items":null,"icon":"leaf","at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":4,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"intro-1","narration":"Here's our plan. First, Plants Make Their Own Food. Then, Inside the Leaf Kitchen. And finally, Why It Matters to Us.","sig":"KBI6684-6MSWKWCLCUjzjUo9hfoJqjpD","actions":[{"id":"agenda","kind":"list","cue":"Here's our plan","text":null,"items":["Plants Make Their Own Food","Inside the Leaf Kitchen","Why It Matters to Us"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":7,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c1","kind":"chapter","title":"Plants Make Their Own Food","segments":[{"id":"c1-0","narration":"Many people think plants eat soil through their roots, just like we eat food. Actually, that is not how it works.","sig":"P0xXMEVfFPbVoeZXLVDg4kaeVQ8KmLZ7","actions":[{"id":"leaf","kind":"icon","cue":"plants eat soil","text":"Leaf","items":null,"icon":"leaf","at":{"col":5,"row":2,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"soil","kind":"box","cue":"eat soil through","text":"Eating Soil","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":4,"w":2,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"cross1","kind":"cross_out","cue":"not how it works","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"soil","color":"red","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-1","narration":"Instead, a plant builds its own sugar right inside its leaves.","sig":"IF6XBboxdg7PBRXL8_g8SNuy129XVZEI","actions":[{"id":"sugar","kind":"box","cue":"builds its own sugar","text":"Builds Sugar","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":4,"w":2,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"check1","kind":"check","cue":"own sugar","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"sugar","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"a0","kind":"arrow","cue":"inside its leaves","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"leaf","to":"sugar","target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-2","narration":"To make that sugar, the leaf only needs three simple ingredients. First, it captures energy from sunlight, and drinks up water.","sig":"5B_DlwpYGR5B7kmW8BdPDUxvPaA4G-eT","actions":[{"id":"sun","kind":"icon","cue":"energy from sunlight","text":"Sunlight","items":null,"icon":"sun","at":{"col":1,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","cue":"energy from sunlight","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"sun","to":"leaf","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null},{"id":"water","kind":"icon","cue":"drinks up water","text":"Water","items":null,"icon":"droplet","at":{"col":5,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"a2","kind":"arrow","cue":"drinks up water","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"water","to":"leaf","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-3","narration":"Finally, it pulls in a gas called carbon dioxide from the air. With those three ingredients, the plant is ready to cook.","sig":"CuGgAky2bONPGSAqtJrweALPT64fB0aZ","actions":[{"id":"co2","kind":"box","cue":"carbon dioxide","text":"CO₂","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":9,"row":1,"w":2,"h":1},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"a3","kind":"arrow","cue":"from the air","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"co2","to":"leaf","target":null,"color":null,"expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c2","kind":"chapter","title":"Inside the Leaf Kitchen","segments":[{"id":"c2-0","narration":"Now that you know plants gather light, water, and carbon dioxide, let us step inside the leaf kitchen to see how they cook them.","sig":"L9rwyLLag_ahhfR57Sa0BaGcuMWj9SEw","actions":[{"id":"recipe","kind":"flow","cue":"inside the leaf kitchen","text":null,"items":["Light + Water + CO₂","Chlorophyll","Sugar + Oxygen"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":10,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-1","narration":"Inside each leaf is a green helper called chlorophyll, which acts like a tiny solar panel trapping sunlight.","sig":"_evC2LRASCsD6aBiur-rJtVx1FUyXP1a","actions":[{"id":"chl_note","kind":"note","cue":"green helper called chlorophyll","text":"Chlorophyll: traps sunlight like a solar panel","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":4,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"hl_chl","kind":"highlight","cue":"trapping sunlight","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"recipe[1]","color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-2","narration":"Using that trapped energy, the leaf rearranges water and carbon dioxide into sweet sugar for food, plus oxygen gas.","sig":"hAq9gTrKxddihtb4BWHY2StYH2zSbdC_","actions":[{"id":"tr1","kind":"trace","cue":"Using that trapped energy","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"recipe","color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"circ_out","kind":"circle_around","cue":"sweet sugar for food","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"recipe[2]","color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-3","narration":"The plant keeps the sugar to grow, and releases the extra oxygen right back into the air.","sig":"XmL_vzQsrgicEHqyzZlixZ7J-t952eau","actions":[{"id":"co_ox","kind":"callout","cue":"extra oxygen right back","text":"Released into the air","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"recipe[2]","color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c3","kind":"chapter","title":"Why It Matters to Us","segments":[{"id":"c3-0","narration":"Now that you have seen how the leaf kitchen makes sugar and oxygen, let us see why it matters to us. Powered by sunlight, plants and animals share a giant loop.","sig":"sl7Stu8ViQQILjAfqyCACEBm9wj4YBJX","actions":[{"id":"sun","kind":"icon","cue":"Powered by sunlight","text":"Sunlight","items":null,"icon":"sun","at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"cycle","kind":"cycle","cue":"share a giant loop","text":null,"items":["Plants make food & O₂","Animals breathe O₂","Animals release CO₂","Plants take in CO₂"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":0,"w":7,"h":5},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","cue":"Powered by sunlight","text":"powers","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"sun","to":"cycle","target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-1","narration":"Plants give us breathable oxygen and the food at the base of almost every food chain. Every bite of fruit or bread is stored sunlight.","sig":"bRl6eKX-rrbU-6UYVPGZ2K-fT9H1PH1L","actions":[{"id":"h1","kind":"highlight","cue":"breathable oxygen","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"cycle[0]","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"h2","kind":"highlight","cue":"stored sunlight","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"cycle[1]","color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-2","narration":"In return, we breathe out carbon dioxide, which plants pull back in to start again. Almost all life on Earth depends on this trade.","sig":"Fc4qD2kNXmUpu20KWt4R-_-uJMKE3QZ6","actions":[{"id":"tr1","kind":"trace","cue":"start again","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"cycle","color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"n1","kind":"note","cue":"Almost all life","text":"Powers almost all life on Earth","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":4,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"purple","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","title":"Recap","segments":[{"id":"recap-0","narration":"So remember: plants make their own food using sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide. Inside their leaves, they cook up sugar and release oxygen for us. Do you have any questions about how it works?","sig":"JM6lgvG3jW9yXv8dP1yjPiPjvksYqg4k","actions":[{"id":"recap_list","kind":"list","cue":"So remember","text":null,"items":["Plants use light, water, and CO₂","Leaves cook sugar and release oxygen","Plants and animals share a loop"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"recap_leaf","kind":"icon","cue":"Inside their leaves","text":"Photosynthesis","items":null,"icon":"leaf","at":{"col":8,"row":2,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]}]}],"quiz":[{"question":"Where do plants actually get their food?","options":["They eat soil through their roots","They make sugar inside their leaves","They absorb sugar from the air","They drink food from rain"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Plants do not eat soil; they build their own sugar inside their leaves using sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide.","chapter":1},{"question":"What is the role of chlorophyll in a leaf?","options":["It traps energy from sunlight","It pulls water up from the roots","It releases carbon dioxide into air","It stores extra sugar for winter"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Chlorophyll acts like a tiny solar panel that traps sunlight so the leaf can cook water and carbon dioxide into sugar.","chapter":2},{"question":"Why do animals depend on photosynthesis?","options":["Plants give us soil to walk on","Plants block harmful sunlight","Plants give us oxygen and food","Plants cool down the air"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Photosynthesis gives us breathable oxygen and the food at the base of almost every food chain.","chapter":3}],"suggestions":["How do plants drink water?","What is cellular respiration?","Why do leaves change color?"],"models":{"lesson":"google/gemini-4-hydrogen","voice":"openai/gpt-audio-mini (marin)"},"createdAt":"2026-11-17T08:00:08.545Z","audioBase":"/samples/photosynthesis"}